Maintenance, outages, spares and return to service (@pe-maintenance: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Electrical-Maintenance-Scheduling-FIST-2026.lingua#r_4Q5B4NW1XVGXWXY6SHP16KKN89", #source "../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC", #source "../sources/Transformer-Maintenance-and-Diagnostics-FIST.lingua#r_5Y3NB9GQFCVNJ8QVR9BC53JS32", #source "../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR", #electrical-power-engineering "Operating-state-handover-events-and-restoration-evidence.lingua#r_6EVVYWESWD36PC42HCGF4ZBQJG") { r_7DVW7TWDKKPHWD780FYGQDCHFB
**Read:** [Maintenance Scheduling for Electrical Equipment — FIST 4-1B](../sources/Electrical-Maintenance-Scheduling-FIST-2026.lingua#r_4Q5B4NW1XVGXWXY6SHP16KKN89), entire current identified document and conditions; [Conduct of power operations and maintenance — FIST](../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC), both whole manuals; [Transformer maintenance and diagnostics — FIST 3-30 and 3-31](../sources/Transformer-Maintenance-and-Diagnostics-FIST.lingua#r_5Y3NB9GQFCVNJ8QVR9BC53JS32), complete applicable method with schedule precedence preserved; [Improving Motor and Drive System Performance — DOE](../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR), whole repair/selection/economics context.

Maintenance preserves or restores a defined function under actual duty, condition and consequence. Calendar, usage, condition and risk-based choices have different evidence needs. Identify the failure mechanism, measurable indicators, task, required competence/tools/spares, outage conditions and test confirming the intended return state.

Read all of [Maintenance Scheduling for Electrical Equipment — FIST 4-1B](../sources/Electrical-Maintenance-Scheduling-FIST-2026.lingua#r_4Q5B4NW1XVGXWXY6SHP16KKN89) and the applicable complete [Conduct of power operations and maintenance — FIST](../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC) manuals. Within that institutional set, the newer schedule overrides equipment-manual intervals; elsewhere, actual current requirements and manufacturer/engineering evidence govern. Do not convert a historical interval into a universal rule.

Compare preventive work with a condition-triggered or repair/replace alternative, including shared dependencies and common-mode maintenance errors. A spare is useful only if compatible, available in time, stored in acceptable condition and installable/testable with the required resources. Reanalyse settings/models after a consequential replacement or changed topology. Preserve the reason for each decision and the measured as-left state. The objective is continuing usable service, with material, technical and human work visible rather than assuming a commissioned plant remains correct indefinitely.

**Continue:** [Operating state, handover, events and restoration evidence](Operating-state-handover-events-and-restoration-evidence.lingua#r_6EVVYWESWD36PC42HCGF4ZBQJG).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
